# Make ConfigField a self-contained nanopb static struct so the same message
# round-trips through the get_custom_behaviors response encode AND (from M3) a
# set request decode (requests are decoded generically, with no per-field
# callbacks). The repeated submessage lists in the RESPONSE — CustomBehaviors.
# behaviors and CustomBehavior.config — stay nanopb callbacks (encoded one entry
# at a time, mirroring combos' encode_combos) so no large arrays sit on the stack.
#
# SetCustomBehaviorRequest.config is the one repeated ConfigField that is DECODED
# (not encoded), so it must be a static array. The decoded zmk_studio_Request is a
# stack local on the RPC thread (rpc.c rpc_main), so config's max_count × the
# ConfigField struct size is charged straight to that thread's stack. Keep both
# small: 8 fields covers hold-tap's scalar set with headroom, and EnumOptions is
# tightened to 5×24 (flavor has 4 names, longest "tap-unless-interrupted" = 22)
# so each ConfigField stays light. ZMK_STUDIO_RPC_THREAD_STACK_SIZE is bumped
# under ZMK_BEHAVIOR_RUNTIME_EDITING to absorb the array (see app/src/studio/Kconfig).
zmk.behaviors.CustomBehavior.display_name max_size:48
zmk.behaviors.CustomBehavior.kind max_size:24
zmk.behaviors.SetCustomBehaviorRequest.config max_count:8
# AddCustomBehaviorRequest is decoded (request), so its strings + config array
# are nanopb-static (same stack-local cost as SetCustomBehaviorRequest — see
# below). kind/display_name match CustomBehavior's sizes; config matches the set
# request's headroom.
zmk.behaviors.AddCustomBehaviorRequest.kind max_size:24
zmk.behaviors.AddCustomBehaviorRequest.display_name max_size:48
zmk.behaviors.AddCustomBehaviorRequest.config max_count:8
zmk.behaviors.ConfigField.key max_size:32
zmk.behaviors.ConfigField.display_name max_size:48
zmk.behaviors.EnumOptions.names max_count:5 max_size:24
zmk.behaviors.KeyPositions.positions max_count:32
